A link back to the source page listed in manifest.json is enough for "appropriate
credit" in most cases, and it is what makes the attribution useful to a reader who
wants to check the derivation.

The values are derived from published standards and are provided as-is, without
warranty of any kind. They are a reference for checking work, not a substitute for
the standards themselves. See README.md for provenance per dataset.
